        "name": null,
        "sourceIndex": 0,
        "steps": [
          {
            "sourceIndex": 0,
            "text": "Separate egg yolks from egg whites. Whisk egg yolks with sugar (50 g).",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:11825"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 1,
            "text": "When the sugar is dissolved add vanilla extract and mix well.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:11826"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 2,
            "text": "In a mixer bowl, whisk together very cold sour cream and heavy cream together until fluffy. Add sugar and continue whisking until firm (don't over whip).",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:11837"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 3,
            "text": "Using a spatula, combine egg yolks with whipped cream together.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:11827"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 4,
            "text": "In a separate bowl, beat the egg whites with a pinch of salt until stiff.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:11828"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 5,
            "text": "With a spatula, carefully combine egg whites with whipped cream.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:11829"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 6,
            "text": "You should get a nice fluffy cream.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:11830"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 7,
            "text": "Spread the cream evenly into a silicone pan or salad bowl.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:11838"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 8,
            "text": "Cover with plastic wrap and refrigerate for 6 hours or overnight.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:11831"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 9,
            "text": "Rinse and drain fresh berries and puree until smooth.\nIf you are using a frozen berries, place them in a leak-proof container and set the container in cold water for 10-15 minutes, then puree them.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:11835"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 10,
            "text": "Pass the puree through a fine sieve to remove all tiny seeds. Coulis is ready.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:11836"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 11,
            "text": "Remove it from the silicone pan and return it back to freezer until serving. (If you used a salad bowl, place it into hot water for a couple seconds). Prepare fresh berries for garnish.",
            "mediaId": null
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 12,
            "text": "Right before serving, pour the coulis over the ice cream cake and garnish with fresh berries.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:11839"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
